// expect: refuse E_EffectMismatch
// A function that stops the program on purpose says so in its row: `chase`
// calls `trap` once it has followed a thousand links, so a `main` that says
// it never traps is refused, and the refusal names the call.
fn chase(depth) = if depth > 1000 { trap() } else { chase(depth + 1) }

fn main() with !Trap = chase(0)
